@H@T0DINFO - Display disk informationImportant:    This   program    is  public    domain  and  may  be  used  and              distributed freely as long as the "Distribution_Rules" are  met              (see subtopic in this help file).Syntax:       DINFO [<options>] {<device name> [<options>]}              Note: The syntax is identical to that of the OS9  free  utility              (except for the additional options -l -e -f).Function:     Displays information about one ore multiple disk devices. If no              device name is specified, the current working directory's  disk              will be used. The main advantage of DINFO over FREE is that  it              displays disk spaces not only in terms of sectors but  also  in              kilobytes and percentage of total disk capacity. Three options,              -e,-f and -l allow more  information  (general,  fragmentation,              block list) to be displayed.Usage:        DINFO                     Displays  information  about  the  current  disk  device                     (= the disk device containing the current directory)              DINFO <disk device name>                     Displaus information about the specified disk.              DINFO <disk device> <disk device>                     More than one device name can be specified.@D1Options : 2Distribution_Rules : 6@T2   -?                    Show short help text.   -e                    Show extended information. This includes disk  type,                         owner, attributes, cluster size and presence and LSN                         of the bootfile.   -f[[=]clusters]       Show the number of blocks that are smaller than  the                         specified  number  of  clusters  (if  no  number  is                         specified, a default of  4  clusters  is  used)  and                         display the space occupied by those "small  blocks".                         This is useful to detect fragmentation of a disk.   -l                    Show a list of all free blocks on the disk. The list                         includes block size in sectors, clusters, KBytes and                         percentage of disk capacity as well as number of the                         first and the last sector in the block.   -b[=]<n>[k]           Give  DINFO   more   memory   for   allocation   map                         examination. For huge disks, this might decrease the                         execution time of DINFO.@T6******************************************************************  DINFO (c) 1989 by Lukas Zeller, CH-Maennedorf                **    email:   zeller@strati.ethz.ch, zeller@ethz.uucp           **             ..!macvax!cernvax!chx400!ethz!zeller              **    DECMail: PSI%4991108411::STRATI::ZELLER                    **    OS9-BBS: LZELLER                                           ******************************************************************This DINFO utility is public domain and may be used and distributed freely  aslong as the following conditions are met: 1.  This Program may only be used for peaceful applications. I do NOT  ALLOW     using this pogram for anything that has to do with development,  testing     or manufacturing of weapons of any type. 2.  This text as well as all copyright messages (in  the  source  text,  the     code and in this help file) must be retained.For bug reports, comments and suggestions, please  contact  the  author  (seeemail paths above). Thank you !